-   entry .apply   `Series(name)(points*)`: a series named by any showable value, with its points
-       The name is shown once, at construction: `Series(t"north")(…)`, `Series(2024)(…)` or
-       `Series(Quarter.Q1)(…)` all give a `Text` name.
-   entry #name   the series' name, as text: its legend entry
-   entry #points   the points, in the order given
-       A line chart sorts them by abscissa before drawing; a scatter plot and a bar chart keep
-       the order, which for bars is the order categories first appear.
-   entry #add   the series with one more point, appended in amortized constant time
-   entry #categorical   the same points with each abscissa as a `Category`, for a bar chart over a numeric axis
-       Needs `x is Showable`. A series over input sizes becomes a bar per size rather than a
-       line over sizes: `timings.categorical.chart(Bars())`.
